<h2>Where should the filters live?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Event type (nine fixed types) and date range (last 24 hours / 7 days / 30 days / 90 days). The page panel is 960px wide and the table has six columns. Each option uses only existing components from 02 Components.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px">Account activity</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:8px">
          <div><div class="label">Date range</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:110px">Last 90 days ▾</div></div>
          <div style="flex:1"><div class="label">Event type</div>
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:2px 8px">
              <span>☑ Sign-in</span><span>☑ Sign-in failed</span><span>☑ Sign-out</span>
              <span>☑ Session expired</span><span>☑ Password changed</span><span>☑ Two-factor enabled</span>
              <span>☑ Email change req.</span><span>☑ Settings updated</span><span>☑ API token used</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:4px;color:#666">Showing 42 of 42 events</div>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:70px">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Filter panel above the table, always open</h3>
      <p>Uses Select and Checkbox list. Every option is visible and needs no extra clicks. It takes the most vertical space, about 4 lines before the table.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px">Account activity</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:6px">
          <div><div class="label">Date range</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:110px">Last 90 days ▾</div></div>
          <button class="mock-button" style="font-size:11px">Event types (all) ▾</button>
          <span style="margin-left:auto;color:#666">Showing 42 of 42 events</span>
        </div>
        <div style="border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;padding:6px;width:170px;margin:0 0 6px 120px;background:#fff">
          ☑ Sign-in<br>☑ Sign-in failed<br>☑ Sign-out<br>… 6 more
        </div>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:60px">Table</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Compact bar, event types in a popover</h3>
      <p>Uses Select, Popover, and Checkbox list. A single line sits above the table. Finding failed sign-ins takes three clicks: open, clear all, check one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div style="padding:12px;font-size:12px">
        <div style="font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px">Account activity</div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:6px">
          <div><div class="label">Date range</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:110px">Last 90 days ▾</div></div>
          <div><div class="label">Event type</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:150px">All events ▾</div></div>
          <span style="margin-left:auto;color:#666">Showing 4 of 42 events</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:#666;margin-bottom:6px">Event type options: All events, Failed sign-ins, Sign-ins and sign-outs, Security changes, …each of the nine types</div>
        <div class="placeholder" style="height:60px">Table</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Two Selects, one value each</h3>
      <p>Uses Select only, with grouped options. It's the simplest and failed sign-ins is a single choice. It can't combine types, for example "password changed + two-factor enabled". The group names would be new copy for reviewers to check.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
